		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Re: When the external rigid body moves, the collision objects inside the rigid body leak out]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=42971#p42971"><![CDATA[
The simplest way would be to use a <strong class="text-strong">btConvexHullShape</strong> for each cuboid wall and assemble them into a <strong class="text-strong">btCompoundShape</strong>.  The points for each convex hull would be the eight corners of the wall box, and you could let all the points be in the local-frame of the <strong class="text-strong">btCompoundShape</strong>, so you could supply identity transform for each subshape's parent-relative transform.  You can make the walls as thick as you like by picking the right points.  Note it is ok, and probably better, if the walls overlap at the corners --&gt; the stuff on the inside will be less likely to escape.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=11033">drleviathan</a> — Sun Jun 28, 2020 9:46 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
